    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1242">

                <pb facs="1286" n="1274" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/11–645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-06T18:00:00+02:00">November 6, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1421. While I have not as yet asked anyone at FonOff what they think of our
                    proposal concerning Straits, I have been told by various well-informed Turks,
                    including newspapermen and a deputy who is a member of Foreign Affairs Committee
                    of National Assembly, that proposal has been very favorably received by Turkish
                    Government. This afternoon parliamentary group of People’s Party is meeting to
                    hear explanation by Foreign Minister of our proposal.<anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d1242-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Dept as 1421; repeated to London as 122 and Moscow as 97.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1242-f1" n="93" xml:id="d1242-f1-content">
                <p>In his telegram 1423, November 8, 11 a.m., Ambassador Wilson reported to the
                    Department that “PriMin said to me last night he finds our proposal for revision
                    Montreux Convention ‘excellent’ and he is ‘greatly pleased’ with it. He added
                    that he believed British ‘are in no hurry’ regarding this matter.”
                    (767.68119/11–845)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
